  "notes": "West leads the ♦K against 6♠. South must hope spades break 3-2. There will be a certain trump loser and South will have to use dummy's clubs to discard his diamond losers.\n\nThis plan will succeed only if the defender with 3 spades also has 3 or more clubs. After winning the ♦A, South should cash the ♠A and ♠K and then start running the clubs.\n\nIf the defenders' spade and club holdings are as hoped for, the defender with the long trump will not be able to ruff in on dummy's clubs before South's diamond losers are gone. South's ♥2 can later be ruffed in the dummy.\n\nIt would be a mistake to try to ruff the ♥2 before playing clubs. If East is long in spades and short in hearts, he may be able to overruff the dummy and cash a diamond trick.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♦K against 6♠. South must hope spades break 3-2. There will be a certain trump loser and South will have to use dummy's clubs to discard his diamond losers.",
